          "id": "1776708349987",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776708349989_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an information extraction agent.\n\nTask:\nRead the user input: `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`\nExtract these three fields if present:\n\n* `ecoNumber`\n* `itemNumber`\n* `itemStructure`\n\nThe input will usually be a request like:\n“Fetch/View WDS based on ECO number, item, and item structure.”\n\nRules:\n\n1. Identify the ECO number, item number, and item structure from the user input.\n2. Be tolerant of common labels and formats, such as:\n\n   * ECO, ECO number, ECO No, ECO#\n   * Item, Item number, Item No, Item#\n   * Item structure, Structure, Item Structure\n3. Ignore extra words like “Fetch”, “View”, “WDS based on”, or other filler text.\n4. If a field is missing, return `null` for that field.\n5. Do not guess values that are not explicitly present.\n6. Return only valid JSON and nothing else.\n\nOutput format:\n{\n\"ecoNumber\": \"string or null\",\n\"itemNumber\": \"string or null\",\n\"itemStructure\": \"string or null\"\n}\n\nExamples:\n\nInput:\n\"Fetch WDS for ECO 12345, item 67890, structure A1\"\nOutput:\n{\n\"ecoNumber\": \"12345\",\n\"itemNumber\": \"67890\",\n\"itemStructure\": \"A1\"\n}\n\nInput:\n\"View WDS based on ECO number ECO-999, item number ITM-456\"\nOutput:\n{\n\"ecoNumber\": \"ECO-999\",\n\"itemNumber\": \"ITM-456\",\n\"itemStructure\": null\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"itemStructure\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"itemNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"ecoNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
