          "code": "SHOW_AFFECTED_ECOS",
          "id": "1776712080349",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776712080350_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input JSON: {{$context.$nodes.GET_WD_DATA.$output.items}} \n\nfor component description use EcoAffectedComponents\n\nAffectedWorkOrderCount for priority.\n\nPlease keep the heading to be: **ECOs for Item number {{$context.$nodes.DERIVE_ITEM_AND_STRUCTURE.$output.itemNumber}}  and  Structure {{$context.$nodes.DERIVE_ITEM_AND_STRUCTURE.$output.structureName}} **\n\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_FORMATTED_DATE.$output.result}} already contains the final display date string.\nUse it exactly as provided in the summary.\nDo not hardcode any sample date.\nDo not convert or reformat it again.\nDo not show any raw ISO date.\n\nThe summary should be of the example: **\"This panel highlights the  ECOs  implemented from {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_FORMATTED_DATE.$output.result}} \"**\n\nDo not do any filtering on your own. The input is already flattened. Follow the structure exactly as it appears in each record.\n\n## Data shape (authoritative)\n\nEach item in the input array is already one flattened row with these fields:\n\n- ChangeNotice\n- ChangeLineId\n- ItemNumber\n- BillSequenceId\n- AlternateBomDesignator\n- EcoAffectedComponents[]\n- AffectedWorkOrderCount\n\n## IMPORTANT RULES\n\n- ItemNumber is the item number from the change line level.\n- ComponentItem is NOT the item number.\n- Never use ComponentItem as Item Number.\n- The ora.Agent call must pass the root-level ItemNumber field only.\n\n## Goal\n\nCreate exactly one MultiRecordWidget row per input record.\n\n## Row fields\n\n- ECO Number: ChangeNotice  \n  Fallback: \"Unknown ECO\"\n\n- Item Number: ItemNumber  \n  Fallback: \"Unknown Item\"\n\n- Item Structure: AlternateBomDesignator  \n  Fallback: \"Unknown Structure\"\n\n- Description:  \n  Summarize only the components in EcoAffectedComponents[].  \n  Do not mention ECO, change, or any date in the description.  \n\n  Use only these fields from each component:\n  - ComponentItem  \n  - ComponentQuantity  \n  - PrimaryUomCode  \n  - ComponentType  \n\n  Format each component like this:  \n  \"Component <ComponentItem>, Qty <ComponentQuantity> <PrimaryUomCode>, Type <ComponentType>\"\n\n  If multiple components exist, join them with \"; \".\n\n  If EcoAffectedComponents[] is empty or missing:  \n  \"No affected components found.\"\n\n- Impact:  \n  Derive this from AffectedWorkOrderCount.  \n  If AffectedWorkOrderCount > 0 → **High**  \n  If AffectedWorkOrderCount <= 0 → **Low**\n\n## Action — STRICT BINDING\n\nCreate only one action per row. Do not create duplicates.\n\nUse this exact action object:\n\n{\n\"text\": \"View Impacted Work Definitions\",\n\"command\": \"ora.Agent({\\\"actionType\\\":\\\"fetchImpactedWorkDefinitions\\\",\\\"data\\\":{\\\"billSequenceId\\\":\\\"<BILL_SEQUENCE_ID>\\\",\\\"changeLineId\\\":\\\"<CHANGE_LINE_ID>\\\",\\\"ChangeNotice\\\":\\\"<CHANGE_NOTICE>\\\",\\\"ItemNumber\\\":\\\"<ITEM_NUMBER>\\\"}})\"\n}\n\n## Binding rules\n\n- <BILL_SEQUENCE_ID> = BillSequenceId  \n- <CHANGE_LINE_ID> = ChangeLineId  \n- <CHANGE_NOTICE> = ChangeNotice  \n- <ITEM_NUMBER> = ItemNumber  \n- If ChangeLineId is null, set \"changeLineId\": null  \n- Never swap billSequenceId and changeLineId  \n- Never use ComponentItem in the action payload  \n\n## Output\n\nReturn only the MultiRecordWidget-ready list of rows, one per input record.  \nDo not include explanations or extra text."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
